    {
      "text": "whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her, Matt. 5:28 (3 Ne. 12:28; D&C 42:23; 63:16). looking up to heaven, he blessed, and brake, Matt. 14:19 (Mark 6:41; Luke 9:16). in a day when he looketh not for him, Matt. 24:50 (Luke 12:46; JS—M 1:53). Master, I beseech thee, look upon my son, Luke 9:38. hand to the plough, and looking back, Luke 9:62. a Levite … came and looked on him, and passed by, Luke 10:32. look on the fields … already to harvest, John 4:35. But he … looked up steadfastly into heaven, Acts 7:55. Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing, Titus 2:13. unto them that look for him shall he appear, Heb. 9:28. he looked for a city which hath foundations, Heb. 11:10. Looking unto Jesus, Heb. 12:2. Looking for and hasting unto the coming of the day of God, 2 Pet. 3:12. look for new heavens and a new earth, 2 Pet. 3:13. Look to yourselves, that we lose not those things, 2 Jn. 1:8. looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ, Jude 1:21.",
